# Experiments content

Runbook: `src/data/EXPERIMENTS.md`.

## Pipeline

1. Place `*.mp4` in `src/assets/experiments/videos/` (filename = JSON `video` value).
2. Append object to `src/data/experiments.json`.
3. `experiments.ts` fills `videoUrl` via glob — never put `videoUrl` in JSON.

## JSON fields

`id`, `title`, `log` (e.g. `"19/52"`), `description`, `url`, `image`, `video`, `kind` (`image` | `music` | `video`), `tags[]`, `date` (`YYYY-MM-DD`), `body`.

- `video`: filename or `null`
- `url` / `image`: usually `null` unless linking out

## UI (preserve unless redesigning)

- Code: `src/features/experiments/` (`BrowserField`, `BrowserComponent`, Matter heap, CRT exit)
- Page: `Experiments.tsx` → `BrowserField` only
- Hover → muted looping video; click → focus; others tumble to heap
- Exit → CRT wipe (`browser-crt-wipe` in CSS)

Prefer JSON + assets over rewriting physics/chrome unless asked.
